  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}). Related noun: {滞|とどこお}り (delay, stagnation).\n\nUSAGE:\n{滞|とどこお}る is used for things that should be moving or progressing but have stopped or slowed. Common contexts:\n- {支払|しはら}いが{滞|とどこお}る - payments fall behind\n- {仕事|しごと}が{滞|とどこお}る - work stagnates\n- {流|なが}れが{滞|とどこお}る - flow stagnates\n\nWRITING:\nOften written as {滞|とどこお}る with the kanji. Can also be written as とどこおる in hiragana.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {捗|はかど}る - to make progress\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {滞納|たいのう} - delinquent payment, arrears\n- {停滞|ていたい} - stagnation, standstill\n\nREGISTER:\nNeutral to formal. Often used in official or business contexts.",
